5. S3 Bucket Temporary access

To provide temporary access to a specific S3 object without giving full bucket permissions, 
I use a pre-signed URL. A pre-signed URL is generated using AWS SDK or CLI, and it includes temporary credentials that allow anyone 
with the URL to download (or upload, if configured) the object for a limited time.
Example : aws s3 presign s3://my-bucket/my-object.txt --expires-in 3600   (3600 sec = 1hr)

6. Continous Delivery Vs Deployment
For example, in a project I worked on, our team used Jenkins pipelines for a web application. 
Every developer commit triggered automated build, unit tests, and integration tests. In Continuous Delivery, 
the pipeline would prepare the artifact and notify the team, and we would manually approve deployment to staging or production. 
In Continuous Deployment, after passing all tests, the artifact was automatically deployed to the staging and production environment 
using Docker and Kubernetes, without any manual approval. This allowed us to release new features quickly while keeping production stable.

7. Jenkins Architecture
 Jenkins follows a master-agent (controller-agent) architecture. The Jenkins master is the main server that manages the build environment, 
schedules jobs, and monitors agents. It handles the web UI, stores configuration, and keeps track of the build history.

8. Agent in Jenkins
The Jenkins agents (or nodes/slaves) are separate machines that perform the actual build, 
test, or deployment tasks assigned by the master. Agents allow Jenkins to distribute workload, which helps in running multiple 
jobs in parallel and on different platforms. The master communicates with agents over a secure channel and sends them the job instructions 
along with the workspace and required code.

9. How Jenkins Know which agent we need to use? 
When we have multiple Jenkins agents (nodes) on Linux, Jenkins decides which agent to use based on job configuration and labels. 
Each agent can be assigned a label, which is like a tag describing its environment or capabilities, for example linux, docker, or high-memory.

